package mcpserver

// Keep task selection and interpretation guidance in the tool descriptions;
// field-specific syntax and constraints also live in the input/output schemas.
const queryGuidance = `

Scope and dates: All views accept applications, users, departments and locations. get_usage and get_activity also accept providers and models. Filter values within one field are ORed; different fields are ANDed. Applications means the calling application, not an MCP server, plugin or model. Use an application ID or directory alias, never guess an ID from a display name such as "chat". To discover observed application IDs and names, call get_usage with group_by=application for the requested period and paginate if needed; this lists observed usage, not an inventory. "Only chat" needs applications; "only my usage" additionally needs a known user ID/email/alias in users. The authenticated admin is not automatically applied as a user filter. Each filter accepts at most 100 nonempty values. Unknown filter values return empty results; there is no fuzzy name search.

from/to are inclusive RFC3339 bounds; defaults are the last 24 hours. Set explicit bounds for calendar periods, comparisons and pagination. Each window is at most 90 days; split longer periods into non-overlapping windows. Buckets align to UTC. Never sum per-period distinct-user/agent counts into a unique total. Trends allow at most 2,000 points; use daily buckets or narrower ranges/filters if exceeded. Every response is {query,warnings,data}; show applicable warnings and use query to verify the applied scope. Empty optional fields may be omitted. Queries have a 30-second deadline; narrow the range or filters after a timeout.`

const usageDescription = `Query AI spending, tokens, provider-call volume and observed user adoption. Use this for FinOps cost-per-user and cost-per-department tables, daily active users, model/application cost comparisons and prompt-size distributions.

Choose a view:
- Default (view=usage, no group_by or interval): data.totals for the selected period.
- group_by=user|department|location|application|model: data.groups ranked by cost descending, then ID ascending. User groups include id and, when available, name, department and location. Empty ID means unassigned. This is the FinOps token/cost ledger; groups have no request counts.
- interval=auto|hour|day: data.totals and data.points per UTC bucket and model. Sum model costs within a bucket for organization-wide daily cost. Missing buckets mean absent telemetry, not a known zero.
- view=adoption, interval=day: daily active_users, new_users, returning_users and requests in data.adoption.points; data.adoption.totals counts distinct users across the whole window; frequency counts users by number of active UTC days. interval defaults to auto. Observed identities are deduplicated through directory aliases; anonymous calls and known application principals are excluded. These are not licensed-employee counts. New means first observed provider activity in retained history under the same filters, not signup; retention can remove older history. Do not sum daily active_users for a period's unique users. single_day_users/repeat_day_users describe activity within this window, not future abandonment.
- group_by=prompt_size: data.prompt_sizes contains totals and ordered input-token size bins to compare request_percent with cost_percent. Sizes include cached input; output-only calls are excluded. Cost shares describe known estimated spend and can be incomplete.

Pagination: Only ranked group_by views support limit (default 20, max 100) and offset (default 0). Pass data.next_offset as the next offset until it is absent; truncated means more rows follow. Keep explicit from/to, all filters, group_by and limit fixed. data.totals and total_groups always cover all matching groups, not just the page. Each call reads current data; late telemetry or directory updates can change rankings between pages. group_by cannot be combined with interval, and adoption cannot be combined with group_by.

Accounting: requests are token-bearing provider calls, not conversations. input_tokens includes cache_read_tokens and cache_creation_tokens; output_tokens includes reasoning_tokens; total_tokens=input_tokens+output_tokens. cost_usd and cache_savings_usd are estimates at stored catalog prices, not invoices; unpriced_tokens>0 means costs are incomplete. Per-call averages and percentages (0 to 100) are pooled and omitted when undefined. Compare periods with separate calls using identical filters; observations alone do not prove causes.` + queryGuidance

const categoriesDescription = `Query what people use AI for: ranked conversation topics, category mix by department, or topic trends. Use get_usage for cost or active users; no costs are attributed to categories.

Default (group_by=category): data.total_prompts and data.categories with category, prompts and share_percent. group_by=department adds department to each row and computes shares within that department; empty department means unassigned. limit defaults to 20, maximum 100; total_categories and totals cover all rows, while truncated signals omitted rows. This tool has no offset pagination.

interval=auto|hour|day returns data.points with time, category, prompts and share_percent instead of ranked categories. Shares are within each bucket. group_by and interval cannot be combined. Only buckets with data are returned; missing buckets are absent telemetry, not a known zero.

Counts cover matched winning categories, exclude risk checks, and represent classified prompts rather than all activity. One winning category counts per classified prompt. Category IDs come from telemetry, not an authoritative topic catalog. Shares range from 0 to 100. No prompt content is returned.` + queryGuidance

const activityDescription = `Query observed executions of custom agents, MCP tools, plugins and built-in tools, matching Customers Activity. Use get_usage for costs, tokens or active users; this tool reports executions rather than an inventory of installed capabilities.

Choose view=summary (default) for totals: distinct_custom_agents, agent_runs, mcp_tool_calls, plugin_executions, builtin_tool_calls and most_used_mcp_tool when available. Select view=agents|mcp|plugins|builtin for that category's totals. For rankings use view=mcp with group_by=server|tool, view=plugins with group_by=plugin, or view=builtin with group_by=tool. Groups rank by executions; limit defaults to 20, maximum 100; total_groups and totals cover all groups and truncated signals omitted rows. Plugin groups include bounded plugin-owned skill details, already included in plugin totals. There is no offset pagination. Summary and agents cannot be grouped.

For trends select a non-summary view and interval=auto|hour|day instead of group_by. data.points contains time, series and executions. MCP series split by server, plugin series by plugin, built-in series by tool. Intervals are zero-filled for observed series; zero means no matching recorded executions, not proof of no usage. Agent series first_observed+other_runs sum to agent_runs. First observed is the earliest identified run across retained history, not creation; that first run must match the selected filters. Other runs include repeats and unidentified runs.

Only non-plugin configured agents count as custom agents; delegated chat helpers are excluded. Distinct agent counts exclude missing IDs. Executions include successful, failed and unreported outcomes; avg_duration_ms is in milliseconds. Plugin attribution overlaps other views: never add plugin executions to tool or agent totals. No private agent or personal-skill names/IDs, user identities, raw traces, prompts or tool arguments are returned.` + queryGuidance
